# EcoTrack/.gitattributes
# Normalises line endings so the repository stays consistent no matter which
# operating system a file was written on.
#
# Windows ends lines with CRLF, Linux and macOS use LF. Without this file, git
# warns on every single commit ("LF will be replaced by CRLF"), and a file saved
# on Windows can show up as entirely rewritten in a diff even when only one line
# actually changed.
#
# "text=auto eol=lf" means: store everything as LF inside the repository, and
# let git convert on checkout. Render and Firebase Hosting both run Linux, so
# LF in the repository is what production wants anyway.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be converted - doing so corrupts them
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
